z@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="269726" owner_email="djkurtz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="63" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/26/269726/63" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I29428919e37e70cd316a87fdcf7ee3e34fe204e7" commit="95a460f264ccf2ca1acc341cf2f77020e178722a" commit_message="CHROMIUM: config: mediatek: enable CONFIG_PWM_MTK_DISP  Enable the dedicated Mediatek PWM driver for driving the backlight of a display.  echo &quot;CONFIG_PWM_MTK_DISP=y&quot; \   &gt;&gt; chromeos/config/arm64/chromiumos-mediatek.flavour.config  echo &quot;CONFIG_PWM_MTK_DISP=y&quot; \   &gt;&gt; chromeos/config/arm64/chromiumos-arm64.flavour.config  chromeos/scripts/kernelconfig oldconfig  Signed-off-by: Eddie Huang &lt;eddie.huang@mediatek.com&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:40578 TEST=build and boot oak-rev1  Change-Id: I29428919e37e70cd316a87fdcf7ee3e34fe204e7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/270749 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="270749" owner_email="djkurtz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="61" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/49/270749/61" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I3b187fdd2ba1798a2ee035cb9e05919f168f3e14" commit="94f8b17bc52b8af4af65464cdb450023fe33cbed" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/img-rogue: add kernel driver from img-ddk 1.6@3710675  Initial commit of IMG DDK kernelmode code.  This patch includes both the SOC-agnostic pieces as well as the SOC-specific code required by the img-rogue driver for the PowerVR GPU on the MT8173 SOC.  This release includes support for DVFS which can be enabled by setting the DRM_POWERVR_ROGUE_DVFS build option.  This release includes in-kernel firmware load support. To enable it, enable CONFIG_DRM_IMG_ROGUE_KERNEL_SRVINIT. You also need to provide a suitable firmware image which is not included here.  This release also adds page fault debugging, (SUPPORT_PAGE_FAULT_DEBUG=1) enabled when you build the driver in debug mode.  To use this feature to its full extent, the usermode driver (img-ddk) must also be built in debug mode with BUILD=debug.  For example, if using portage:   USE=img_debug emerge-{b} img-ddk).  Signed-off-by: Rufus Hamade &lt;rufus.hamade@imgtec.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Chiawen Lee &lt;chiawen.lee@mediatek.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Frank Binns &lt;frank.binns@imgtec.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:39263 BUG=chrome-os-partner:39455 BUG=chrome-os-partner:40578 BUG=chrome-os-partner:41780 BUG=chrome-os-partner:42626 BUG=chrome-os-partner:45469 BUG=chrome-os-partner:44447 TEST=build and boot oak-rev2 &amp; -rev3 TEST=Boot Oak board to Freon UI, login and browse BBC website. TEST=Run glbench.  Run glmark2.  Look for errors in dmesg.  Change-Id: I3b187fdd2ba1798a2ee035cb9e05919f168f3e14 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/277641 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="277641" owner_email="rufus.hamade@imgtec.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="31" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/41/277641/31" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I63fe84d94b272708a7f9d6